IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law (8 Del. C. ch. 1), section 213: fixing the date for the determination of stockholders of
-- record. Layer 1, from the text alone. Quote lines are copied from de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt by script.
--
-- A record date is a day: "the close of business on" that day is what the text means, and a stockholder of record
-- at that moment is a person who held of record on that day and had not ceased to by the close of business.
-- Scope for nonstock corporations: s 215(a) says s 213 does not apply to them; s 215(f) has its own record-date rule.

§ `s 213 Fixing date for determination of stockholders of record`

§§ `s 213(a) The record date for a meeting`

-- The board may fix a record date, which shall not precede the date the resolution fixing it is adopted, and shall not be
-- more than 60 nor less than 10 days before the date of the meeting. Both ends count (fork F-D).
-- src:789 | In order that the corporation may determine the stockholders entitled to notice of any meeting of stockholders or any adjournment thereof, the board of directors may fix a record date, which record date shall not precede the date upon which the resolution fixing the record date is adopted by the board of directors, and which record date shall not be more than 60 nor less than 10 days before the date of such meeting. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(a) (src:789)
GIVEN `the day proposed as the record date` IS A DATE
      `the day the board adopts the resolution fixing the record date` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 213(a) the board of directors may fix the day as the record date for the meeting` `the day proposed as the record date` `the day the board adopts the resolution fixing the record date` `the day of the meeting` MEANS
        `the day proposed as the record date` AT LEAST `the day the board adopts the resolution fixing the record date`
    AND `the day proposed as the record date` AT LEAST (`the date` (`period in days` 60) `before` `the day of the meeting`)
    AND `the day proposed as the record date` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 10) `before` `the day of the meeting`)

-- If the board fixes a date, it is also the record date for voting at the meeting, unless the board determines, at the time
-- it fixes it, that a later date on or before the date of the meeting shall be the date for that determination.
-- If no record date is fixed, the record date for notice and for voting is the close of business on the day next
-- preceding the day notice is given or, if notice is waived, the close of business on the day next preceding the day of the
-- meeting. A "later date" must be later than the date fixed and not after the meeting; anything else is not covered.
-- src:789 | If the board of directors so fixes a date, such date shall also be the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote at such meeting unless the board of directors determines, at the time it fixes such record date, that a later date on or before the date of the meeting shall be the date for making such determination. If no record date is fixed by the board of directors, the record date for determining stockholders entitled to notice of and to vote at a meeting of stockholders shall be at the close of business on the day next preceding the day on which notice is given, or, if notice is waived, at the close of business on the day next preceding the day on which the meeting is held. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(a) (src:789)
GIVEN `the record date the board fixed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day notice is given` IS A DATE
      `notice is waived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 213(a) the record date for the stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting` `the record date the board fixed` `the day notice is given` `notice is waived` `the day of the meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the record date the board fixed`
    WHEN JUST fixed THEN fixed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `notice is waived`
        THEN `the day of the meeting` MINUS 1
        ELSE `the day notice is given` MINUS 1

@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(a) (src:789)
GIVEN `the record date the board fixed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the later date the board determined, when it fixed the record date, to be the date for determining who votes` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day notice is given` IS A DATE
      `notice is waived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 213(a) the record date for the stockholders entitled to vote at the meeting` `the record date the board fixed` `the later date the board determined, when it fixed the record date, to be the date for determining who votes` `the day notice is given` `notice is waived` `the day of the meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the record date the board fixed`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`s 213(a) the record date for the stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting` NOTHING `the day notice is given` `notice is waived` `the day of the meeting`)
    WHEN JUST fixed THEN
        CONSIDER `the later date the board determined, when it fixed the record date, to be the date for determining who votes`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST fixed
        WHEN JUST later THEN
            IF later GREATER THAN fixed AND later AT MOST `the day of the meeting`
